    <briefdescription>
<para>Heuristic language detector based on stopword frequency analysis. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Tokenises <computeroutput>text</computeroutput> into lower-cased whitespace-separated words and counts how many belong to the stopword sets for each candidate language (currently English and German). The language with the highest match ratio above a configurable confidence threshold wins.</para>
<para>Supported languages and their ISO 639-1 codes:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>"en"</computeroutput> — English (uses <computeroutput>utils::Stopwords::defaults("en")</computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>"de"</computeroutput> — German (uses <computeroutput>utils::Stopwords::defaults("de")</computeroutput>)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>For text that matches neither set above the threshold, the result is <computeroutput>"und"</computeroutput> (undetermined).</para>
<para><heading level="3">Accuracy expectations</heading>
</para>
<para><table rows="5" cols="2"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Condition  </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Expected result  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>≥ 10 English stopwords in a 100-word sample  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>"en"</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>≥ 10 German stopwords in a 100-word sample  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>"de"</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>Very short input (&lt; 3 words)  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>"und"</computeroutput>  </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para>Mixed language / technical text  </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>"und"</computeroutput> or best match  </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para><heading level="3">Performance</heading>
</para>
<para>&lt; 1 ms for a 10 000-character text on a modern CPU.</para>
<para>Thread-safety: all methods are stateless; an instance may be shared. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
